 numerical values that show you the likelihood of certain outcomes. Choose from American, decimal, or fractional odds at Stake."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"afdc6946451b","_type":"table","asset":null,"rows":[{"_key":"2a108cbe-d758-488a-91c8-0dc4c161fb09","_type":"tableRow","cells":["Odds format","How it looks","Understanding this format","How to calculate potential returns"]},{"_key":"9bbb6816-09a0-4d76-b2cf-edacd55ff73c","_type":"tableRow","cells":["Decimal","1.50","The lower the figure, the more likely the outcome. For example, if Serena Williams had odds of 1.40 while Coco Gauff had odds of 2.10, it would mean that Williams is the favourite.","Return = stake x decimal value. ($10 x 1.50 = a return of $15)."]},{"_key":"59acc3aa-4d41-47d1-9f1a-6ff0f1ce320e","_type":"tableRow","cells":["American/Moneyline","+/-1.50","If odds begin with a minus, this will typically indicate the favourite. When odds have a minus, this is how much you will need to bet to win $100. If it begins with a plus symbol, that represents your profit based on a bet of $100.","$10 bet on -150 odds = $16.70 $10 bet on +150 odds = $25.00"]},{"_key":"ae88a9cf-7b9c-432a-865a-38f2c834927f","_type":"tableRow","cells":["Fractional","1.5/1","The first number in fractional odds shows you what your profit would be, presuming the second number is your stake. A lower figure means an outcome is more likely.","$10 bet on 1.5/1 = $25 return ($15 profit and $10 stake)."]}]},{"_key":"ffe008161a28","_type":"block","asset":null,"children":[{"_key":"196eae3e5385","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"How do live tennis odds and scores work?"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"614486e9878d","_type":"block","asset":null,"children":[{"_key":"a6226df5e7e6","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Live or "},{"_key":"b3667af74c0a","_type":"span","marks":["7bad787b14de"],"text":"in-play betting"},{"_key":"a9750cb95621","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":" on tennis shows you up-to-the-moment odds based on the curren